{"id":"572ee888b3bb87a15fb98ca4002b37f501404a70","axis":"silent","repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go","sha":"572ee888b3bb87a15fb98ca4002b37f501404a70","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ This project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.htm"," - Encode an empty attribute value nested in a slice or map as `{}` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace`, so the auto-instrumentation span that carries it is no longer dropped. (#9182)"," - Match the response `Content-Type` media type case-insensitively and ignore parameters when reading OTLP/HTTP protobuf partial-success responses in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp`. (#9188)"," - Do not report an error through the global error handler when `WithCompressor(\"none\")` is passed to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc` or `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetricgrpc`. (#9056)","+- Decode gzip responses with explicitly configured `Accept-Encoding` headers in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp` and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetrichttp`, enforcing response limits after decompression. (#9203)"," - Preserve exemplar trace and span IDs in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus` by dropping filtered attribute labels instead of the whole exemplar when the combined exemplar labels would exceed the prometheus client-go limit. (#9031)"," - Treat `unix-abstract://` endpoints from `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` as insecure in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc` and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp`, matching `unix://` endpoints and the metric exporters. (#9261)"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp/client.go","lines":["@@ -278,23 +278,8 @@ func (c *httpClient) uploadLogs(ctx co